  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Trim has 9 pages: Statement of Net Position (p1), Statement of Activities (p2-3), governmental funds assets/fund balances (p4) and receipts/expenditures (p5), proprietary Statement of Net Position (p6, accrual), proprietary revenues/expenses (p7), cash flows (p8), all-funds budgetary comparison (p9, unaudited). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p5); 'Gain on Sale of Capital Assets' 1,294 is printed inside Total Receipts, so it is a receipt line. Transfers: printed Total-column 'Transfers From (To) Other Funds' 145,920 out, all to the Utilities Fund (General -9,234, Street -5,823, Non-Major -130,863 kept per fund in detail). Business-type from the Proprietary Fund Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p7), measure net position (1,405,968 -> 1,636,190), as in FY2023/FY2024; the government-wide business-type column (p1-3, cash 1,047,030 -> 1,304,868) differs. Proprietary cash flow statement (p8) not recorded (proprietary null as in later years). beginning_cash null (no prior-year cash printed); fund balances from p5; ending cash/investments are sums of the printed governmental cash and investment lines (p4). Balance sheet: governmental lines from p4 (totals equal government-wide p1), business-type lines from p1. Detail per fund column of p5 (General, Street, Non-Major) and the Utilities Fund from p7; the all-funds budgetary comparison (p9, single combined column) is not recorded in detail, as in FY2023. Read pages 1-9 of 9"
}
